<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01389#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: confession-every-sunday-around-brunch-time; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a person in a grey hoodie holding a white cat close to their face, with a text overlay that reads 'confession-every sunday around brunch time' and 'i take my cat to the mall and make people take pictures of us'. The overall intent is to humorously present a mundane, slightly absurd personal ritual as a 'confession', creating a comedic effect through the juxtaposition of a serious-sounding term ('confession') with a trivial, everyday activity. There is no toxicity present. The meme relies on irony and self-deprecating humor, not on targeting or disparaging any group or individual based on protected characteristics. The intent is to entertain by highlighting the quirky nature of the person's behavior, not to harm, abuse, or propagate harmful stereotypes."@en .
