<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01389#semiotic_projection_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The user is projected onto the visual entity 'person' holding the cat, as the meme's text describes a personal, first-person ritual ('confession-every sunday around brunch time') that the user performs. The act of taking the cat to the mall and making people take pictures is framed as a personal confession, implying the user is the one engaging in this behavior. The affectionate visual interaction between the person and the cat reinforces this self-referential projection."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#ComparativePositioning> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#SemanticAdjacency> .
