<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TemplateStructure> <http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#promptExtractionText> "Extract Template Structure elements from the image. Template Structure includes: template patterns, organizational frameworks, structural elements, layout templates, framework components, and structural patterns. For each structural element found, provide: 1) A descriptive instance_name (e.g., 'contrast_template', 'layout_framework'), 2) A natural language label (e.g., 'the contrast template', 'the layout framework'), 3) A brief description of the structural pattern or framework. Focus on the underlying organizational structure of the meme. Example output format: {\"instance_name\": \"contrast_template\", \"label\": \"the contrast template\", \"description\": \"The meme follows a contrast template with calm foreground subject against chaotic background scene\"}"@en .
<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01389#mapping_1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The top text 'confession-every sunday around brunch time' is mapped onto the visual entity 'person', implying that the person is the one performing the 'confession' ritual. The person's affectionate interaction with the cat visually represents the 'confession' activity described in the text."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#EnvironmentalText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Text naturally occurring in the depicted meme scene environment"@en .
